{"messages": [{"id": 14, "from": "A", "in_reply_to": 13, "text": "I agree with the revised list; I don’t know the will or estate facts, so I can’t say who is named or what shares apply. I meant that C’s agreement is important to me before pursuing a family purchase—not that B is or isn’t named. I don’t know yet whether my husband would own part of the house. Please keep him out of these messages for now; I agree not to include him unless all three sisters agree. These messages can stay among us and you.

Before taking a draft to an adviser, I’d need clear price, payment, ownership, cost, occupancy, financing, and closing terms, including what happens if financing fails. I’d ask the estate representative whether a lawful interim distribution for B is possible. B’s need matters to me regardless of what the will says, though the will may determine legal entitlements. I agree silence is not agreement."}, {"id": 16, "from": "B", "in_reply_to": 15, "text": "I don’t know anything about the will’s wording, or who is handling the estate. “Timing matters” means I’d like to know as soon as we can whether money for the studio might be available, but I have no set deadline or amount. Please list an interim distribution as a question for the estate representative, not as something I’m entitled to receive. My need should be heard, though I understand it doesn’t determine my legal share.

The list seems fair to me. Please keep the studio details general, and keep these messages among us four. I agree not to include A’s husband unless all three sisters agree, and that silence isn’t agreement. Before taking terms to an adviser, I’d want the price, payment timing, shares, costs, occupancy, financing, closing date, and what happens if financing fails made clear."}, {"id": 18, "from": "C", "in_reply_to": 17, "text": "I agree with the list. I don’t know what the will says, who has it, or who is handling the estate. I’d consider A buying at full appraised value if the shares, payment timing, and other terms are clear to all three and we’ve had time for advice. B’s need matters, though it doesn’t determine her legal share. Keep these messages among us four for now; don’t include A’s husband unless all three sisters agree. Silence isn’t agreement."}], "turn": 9, "of": 15, "unread": 0}
